Description: A practical toolkit for systematic reviewers conducting
    meta-analyses of proportions, risk ratios, odds ratios, hazard ratios,
    mean differences, correlations, generic inverse-variance effects, and
    incidence rates. Designed to reduce the gap between statistical
    analysis and publication-ready reporting, the package provides a unified
    interface for model fitting, subgroup analysis, meta-regression,
    leave-one-out influence diagnostics, heterogeneity assessment, and
    non-pooling umbrella-review synthesis with primary-study overlap analysis.
    Outputs include formatted summary tables via 'gt', automatically scaled
    forest plots, cumulative forest plots, and comprehensive publication bias
    assessment (Egger and Begg tests, trim-and-fill, contour-enhanced funnel
    plots, limit meta-analysis, and DOI plots).
